{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile-bridge outbound comment sync","key_entities":["REB-1861","comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body","adapters/jira/comment_limits.py","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615","bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f","Actions run 32403944666","712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e","cleanup.py"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira reconciliation","data cleanup","comment deduplication","outbound sync bug","rate limiting","5000-comment cap"],"propositions":["The reconcile-bridge's inert comment-id dedup map caused the outbound sync to re-post identical comments on every hourly pass, accumulating 30,847 duplicate bot-authored comments across 30 Jira issues and pinning REB-1861 at the 5000-comment hard cap.","Phase 1 cleanup deleted 29,931 duplicates by keeping the oldest copy of each distinct normalized comment body (as determined by the reconciler's own normalization function) and removing all later copies, verified independently against pre-deletion backups with zero missing distinct bodies.","Three issues (REB-1567, REB-1931, REB-2605) hold 836 unmarked comments authored by the same bot that lack the reconciler marker due to outbound truncation at 32,767 characters cutting off the marker paragraph; these were deliberately excluded from phase 1 and deferred to a separate evidence-gated phase 2 behind --include-truncated.","All 30,847 marked deletion candidates were identified using pre-strip ADF rendering to preserve the RECONCILER_MARKER before normalization-based deduplication, ensuring bot-authored echoes are reliably distinguished from human comments.","Rate-limiting on 429 responses was handled with explicit retry-after backoff throughout execution (713+ throttles absorbed), and the operation is resumable via an append-only deletion log with zero failed deletions across 29,931 DELETEs.","Post-deletion verification confirmed every distinct normalized body on all 27 affected issues retains exactly one surviving copy, unmarked comment counts are unchanged, and all issues are now far below the 5000-comment cap."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787338727790388001,"uuid":"4b6fdad0-6496-45a2-b519-536bcde73d64"}